1
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:03,693
They're about to exit the tunnel!

2
00:00:06,073 --> 00:00:08,733
No! Not good! Darby's ahead!

3
00:00:08,953 --> 00:00:10,553
And by a full car length!

4
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:12,710
Our speed is about to be doubled!

5
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:14,233
It looks like I win!

6
00:00:16,053 --> 00:00:16,883
No!

7
00:00:16,966 --> 00:00:20,574
The fact of the matter is, I still
have more speed than you, Darby!

8
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:23,333
You're in for it now!

9
00:00:27,493 --> 00:00:28,323
No!

10
00:00:28,406 --> 00:00:29,993
I can't believe what I'm seeing!

11
00:00:31,153 --> 00:00:33,350
Cocculeen had enough power
to spin his car around

12
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:36,139
and knock Darby's car
clear off the racetrack!

13
00:00:36,253 --> 00:00:38,893
He used his speed to
his advantage! Uh-huh!

14
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:40,733
He's out of there!

15
00:00:42,313 --> 00:00:44,901
And Cocculeen's car is
safely on the ground!

16
00:00:45,153 --> 00:00:46,373
You did it!

17
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:49,253
The weaker car loses in a collision.

18
00:00:49,673 --> 00:00:53,110
Giving up power to ram me will
prove to be a costly mistake.

19
00:00:53,193 --> 00:00:54,310
Instead of gloating,

20
00:00:54,393 --> 00:00:56,350
you should have paid more
attention to my plan to stay

21
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:59,433
behind and knock you off
course with a spin attack.

22
00:00:59,793 --> 00:01:03,433
So you say though the same
could also be said of you

23
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:06,453
Losing power was not an accident

24
00:01:07,053 --> 00:01:10,233
You're so self-righteous in your hubris.

25
00:01:10,393 --> 00:01:14,099
You didn't realize I planned for
you to knock my car off course

26
00:01:14,633 --> 00:01:16,613
Everything rests on this

27
00:01:17,273 --> 00:01:18,313
Look closely.

28
00:01:18,513 --> 00:01:20,513
Do you see where my car is headed?

29
00:01:30,373 --> 00:01:34,713
He landed on the other side,
farther ahead at that! Impossible!

30
00:01:36,033 --> 00:01:37,073
Yes, ordinarily.

31
00:01:37,473 --> 00:01:39,090
Even at one's top speed,

32
00:01:39,173 --> 00:01:42,770
a move like the one I just did
usually would result in a crash.

33
00:01:42,853 --> 00:01:45,670
You wouldn't make it by
jumping over the curves.

34
00:01:45,753 --> 00:01:49,577
But it's another story completely
if you're catapulted over them.

35
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:52,113
All I needed was your help.

36
00:01:52,953 --> 00:01:54,850
From the moment we left the tunnel,

37
00:01:54,933 --> 00:01:58,286
my plan was to get you to hit
me by sacrificing my power.

38
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:03,813
That said, I think it's time we
continued our race, don't you?

39
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:08,473
Don't let this guy get to
you, Kakyoin! Stay focused!

40
00:02:14,913 --> 00:02:15,743
Kakyoin!

41
00:02:15,973 --> 00:02:19,393
There, now his soul belongs to me.

42
00:02:19,873 --> 00:02:21,993
The poor fool admitted defeat.

43
00:02:22,693 --> 00:02:26,533
He finally realized that it was
pointless to continue racing.

44
00:02:29,013 --> 00:02:30,333
Still, I must say,

45
00:02:30,753 --> 00:02:34,988
you, Kakyoin, are the first opponent
to ever make me perspire like this.

46
00:02:41,273 --> 00:02:42,833
Given its source material,

47
00:02:43,113 --> 00:02:47,289
this doll will make a most exquisite
addition to my growing collection.

48
00:02:47,853 --> 00:02:51,030
He was the very first opponent
to muster up the courage to

49
00:02:51,113 --> 00:02:55,054
conquer his fears and resist cracking
under such colossal pressure.

50
00:03:02,533 --> 00:03:06,073
I will treasure his good company always.

51
00:03:08,593 --> 00:03:09,423
Careful,

52
00:03:09,506 --> 00:03:11,410
it would be in the best interest of all

53
00:03:11,493 --> 00:03:14,317
involved for you to keep
your emotions in check.

54
00:03:14,413 --> 00:03:16,413
Harming me is out of the question.

55
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:20,810
You see, dying is something I simply
can't do if you want your friend back.

56
00:03:20,893 --> 00:03:23,270
Slipping on a banana
peel and hitting my head.

57
00:03:23,353 --> 00:03:24,693
choking on gum,

58
00:03:24,893 --> 00:03:28,950
or even suffering a heart attack from
the shock of popping a bag of popcorn.

59
00:03:29,033 --> 00:03:33,853
If any of those things sent me to
heaven, Kakyoin's soul would go too.

60
00:04:01,053 --> 00:04:02,370
I'll

61
00:04:02,453 --> 00:04:08,690
see you

62
00:04:08,773 --> 00:04:09,993
next time.

63
00:04:23,353 --> 00:04:24,213
Goods now

64
00:04:38,493 --> 00:04:45,453
Fuuaku no last page ni So
no kobushi wo Ta taki kome

65
00:04:46,633 --> 00:04:48,073
End of the world

66
00:04:50,073 --> 00:04:51,753
that along Our Our

67
00:04:54,213 --> 00:04:56,593
Our Our Our Our Our

68
00:05:02,893 --> 00:05:03,723
Story

69
00:05:10,073 --> 00:05:10,903
The H

70
00:05:18,793 --> 00:05:19,623
What the?

71
00:05:19,753 --> 00:05:22,133
Hey, Jotaro, wait! What's this?

72
00:05:22,493 --> 00:05:23,513
Hey, Jotaro!

73
00:05:23,813 --> 00:05:25,310
Why the hell are you sitting down?

74
00:05:25,393 --> 00:05:27,390
We should be kicking Geppetto's ass!

75
00:05:27,473 --> 00:05:28,653
I'll play him next!

76
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:32,365
Old man, have you ever actually
played any of these games?

77
00:05:32,493 --> 00:05:35,022
If not, the odds wouldn't
be in your favor.

78
00:05:37,893 --> 00:05:39,390
Stay out of it, old man.

79
00:05:39,473 --> 00:05:42,885
Ben, this isn't your average
game of gin rummy, after all.

80
00:05:44,853 --> 00:05:46,253
We're playing baseball.

81
00:05:46,953 --> 00:05:50,473
That's the game I choose to
settle this once and for all.

82
00:05:52,453 --> 00:05:54,693
As collateral, I'll bet my soul.

83
00:05:55,753 --> 00:05:58,635
Alright, then I would like
to bet Kakyoin's soul.

84
00:06:00,793 --> 00:06:03,433
My stand, Atum, has released your arm.

85
00:06:03,633 --> 00:06:05,574
You may thank me at your leisure.

86
00:06:05,933 --> 00:06:08,593
Now that Kakyoin's soul
is in my collection,

87
00:06:08,873 --> 00:06:12,830
there's no longer reason for me to
keep your arm in my stand's clutches.

88
00:06:12,913 --> 00:06:14,413
And suffice it to say,

89
00:06:14,613 --> 00:06:19,033
I'd be at a bit of a disadvantage if
I faced you with my stand one-handed.

90
00:06:19,353 --> 00:06:23,471
I'm well aware of your Star Platinum's
incredible speed and precision.

91
00:06:25,373 --> 00:06:28,810
Really, out of all the games
you could have chosen to play,

92
00:06:28,893 --> 00:06:33,473
it's unfortunate for you that
we're playing my specialty.

93
00:06:34,053 --> 00:06:34,883
Derby!

94
00:06:35,113 --> 00:06:36,073
Just you wait.

95
00:06:36,193 --> 00:06:38,190
The moment Jotaro wipes
the floor with you,

96
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:40,490
I'll throttle the life
out of your pompous ass.

97
00:06:40,573 --> 00:06:41,867
And that is a promise.

98
00:06:47,473 --> 00:06:49,093
Oh, that's a baseball.

99
00:06:52,993 --> 00:06:55,490
Doesn't look like he's
tempered with this game either.

100
00:06:55,573 --> 00:06:56,632
You're good to go.

101
00:06:57,713 --> 00:07:00,478
Before we begin, you'll
need to pick your team.

102
00:07:03,573 --> 00:07:04,403
Jaguars.

103
00:07:04,973 --> 00:07:05,803
Jaguars!

104
00:07:06,813 --> 00:07:08,093
Yes, I see.

105
00:07:08,433 --> 00:07:11,930
You've decided to go with a team
that has a strong offense, eh?

106
00:07:12,013 --> 00:07:14,366
And two with a batting average over 400.

107
00:07:14,733 --> 00:07:18,110
If that's how you're going to play
it, I'll choose the Red Dragons.

108
00:07:18,193 --> 00:07:19,233
Red Dragons!

109
00:07:20,913 --> 00:07:22,031
Offense or defense?

110
00:07:22,373 --> 00:07:23,693
Go on, take your pick.

111
00:07:25,373 --> 00:07:26,203
Offense.

112
00:07:26,286 --> 00:07:29,513
In that case, the Jaguars will bat first.

113
00:07:30,493 --> 00:07:35,434
Next, you can begin designing your own
players by drawing their faces on the screen.

114
00:07:36,153 --> 00:07:39,393
This handsome devil is Star Platinum.

115
00:07:41,033 --> 00:07:44,770
Now that we've gotten the
preparations out of the way...

116
00:07:44,853 --> 00:07:45,773
Playball!

117
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:51,353
Jaguars versus Red Dragons!

118
00:07:52,453 --> 00:07:53,283
Playball!

119
00:08:01,153 --> 00:08:03,733
I've chosen number 15 as my pitcher.

120
00:08:04,073 --> 00:08:06,249
January 5th is my birthday, you know.

121
00:08:09,673 --> 00:08:11,293
Now, here we go.

122
00:08:11,673 --> 00:08:13,373
The pitcher is winding up!

123
00:08:14,773 --> 00:08:16,273
The first pitch!

124
00:08:18,033 --> 00:08:18,863
What?

125
00:08:21,013 --> 00:08:21,973
Strike one!

126
00:08:22,953 --> 00:08:24,093
Uh, hey!

127
00:08:24,293 --> 00:08:26,053
I don't get it! What's wrong?

128
00:08:26,333 --> 00:08:28,090
That was a pretty amateur move back there.

129
00:08:28,173 --> 00:08:33,114
It's great that you swung the bat and all,
but it was before he even threw the ball!

130
00:08:39,553 --> 00:08:41,593
Hey, what's this all about?

131
00:08:42,033 --> 00:08:45,050
There's no need for you to
practice your swing, is there?

132
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:46,013
Hang on!

133
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:50,633
Jotaro, is this the very first
time you've ever played this?

134
00:08:50,993 --> 00:08:54,287
In fact, have you ever played
a video game in your life?

135
00:08:55,093 --> 00:08:57,473
You answer me right now, Jotaro!

136
00:08:57,993 --> 00:08:58,830
Relax.

137
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:01,031
I already know how to play baseball.

138
00:09:01,293 --> 00:09:03,764
I'll figure out the game controls as I go.

139
00:09:04,673 --> 00:09:06,513
What are you saying?

140
00:09:06,933 --> 00:09:10,010
In case you haven't noticed,
your timing is totally off!

141
00:09:10,093 --> 00:09:11,753
Your swings are pathetic!

142
00:09:12,153 --> 00:09:15,271
Don't lie, this is your
first time playing, isn't it?

143
00:09:24,453 --> 00:09:25,393
Strike two!

144
00:09:27,473 --> 00:09:31,010
And now you're actually swinging the bat
after the catcher has caught the ball!

145
00:09:31,093 --> 00:09:32,790
You don't know what you're doing!

146
00:09:32,873 --> 00:09:34,520
Dammit, Jotaro, I was right!

147
00:09:34,713 --> 00:09:37,630
You don't know a video game
from a hole in the ground!

148
00:09:37,713 --> 00:09:39,013
Strike! Better out!

149
00:09:40,793 --> 00:09:42,690
Jotaro, it's time to get serious!

150
00:09:42,773 --> 00:09:45,150
Stop trying to act cool
and use your blasted head!

151
00:09:45,233 --> 00:09:46,730
You bet your soul on this game,

152
00:09:46,813 --> 00:09:49,410
so if you think you can back
out due to lack of experience,

153
00:09:49,493 --> 00:09:50,323
think again!

154
00:09:50,406 --> 00:09:51,236
Good grief.

155
00:09:51,513 --> 00:09:53,910
This is the worst pep
talk I've ever heard.

156
00:09:53,993 --> 00:09:55,290
You should be more encouraging.

157
00:09:55,373 --> 00:09:59,250
Try something like, it's only the first
inning, you can still make a comeback.

158
00:09:59,333 --> 00:10:01,290
What the hell's going
through that head of yours?

159
00:10:01,373 --> 00:10:05,530
You can't possibly rely solely on Star
Platinum's reflexes to win this game,

160
00:10:05,613 --> 00:10:06,443
can you?

161
00:10:06,526 --> 00:10:07,356
Think about it!

162
00:10:07,439 --> 00:10:09,150
You don't know the first
thing about video games!

163
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:11,174
How are you supposed to beat him?

164
00:10:11,833 --> 00:10:13,304
What's your plan, Jotaro?

165
00:10:13,653 --> 00:10:14,773
Answer me, damn it!

166
00:10:14,973 --> 00:10:17,620
Do you have a way to
beat this weirdo or not?

167
00:10:19,153 --> 00:10:19,983
Jotaro?

168
00:10:21,333 --> 00:10:22,163
Listen,

169
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:25,390
if your strategy is to trick me
by pretending to be an amateur,

170
00:10:25,473 --> 00:10:28,179
let me inform you that
it isn't going to work.

171
00:10:28,933 --> 00:10:31,650
I'd never be foolish enough
to let my guard down.

172
00:10:31,733 --> 00:10:34,610
Even if you were a helpless
child, it wouldn't happen.

173
00:10:34,693 --> 00:10:36,453
A soul is at stake.

174
00:10:37,573 --> 00:10:38,433
Old man.

175
00:10:39,873 --> 00:10:42,579
Since you wanted to know,
I don't have a plan.

176
00:10:43,533 --> 00:10:45,393
However, if I did have one,

177
00:10:45,633 --> 00:10:47,770
the only thing it would
involve would be knocking

178
00:10:47,853 --> 00:10:50,290
the nose straight off the
face of this condescending,

179
00:10:50,373 --> 00:10:53,902
overinflated douchebag of a
prick taking up space beside me.

180
00:10:54,013 --> 00:10:56,837
All I care about is getting
Kakyoin's soul back.

181
00:10:57,253 --> 00:10:58,833
I'll do whatever it takes.

182
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:02,493
You talk a big game,

183
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:05,610
but it's still the top of the
first inning and you have won out.

184
00:11:05,693 --> 00:11:07,293
The match is far from over.

185
00:11:07,573 --> 00:11:09,410
And since you haven't played before,

186
00:11:09,493 --> 00:11:13,573
You should know that if you fall
more than 11 points behind you lose

187
00:11:18,093 --> 00:11:20,513
Second batter number three

188
00:11:24,693 --> 00:11:25,523
Strike

189
00:11:26,053 --> 00:11:28,873
Damn, he's getting even worse that time.

190
00:11:28,993 --> 00:11:31,450
He swung the bat over 40
centimeters above the ball.

191
00:11:31,533 --> 00:11:32,573
How's he so bad?

192
00:11:33,273 --> 00:11:36,473
Strike two what it wasn't even close

193
00:11:40,713 --> 00:11:42,813
Strike three! You're out!

194
00:11:45,433 --> 00:11:46,550
It's all over.

195
00:11:46,633 --> 00:11:49,045
Jotaro's no match for someone like Darby.

196
00:11:49,253 --> 00:11:52,250
This massacre is like being forced
to watch a group of high school

197
00:11:52,333 --> 00:11:56,030
baseball champs go head-to-head
with kids from the knitting club.

198
00:11:56,113 --> 00:11:57,313
It's pathetic!

199
00:11:57,853 --> 00:11:59,713
Strike one! Strike two!

200
00:12:02,353 --> 00:12:03,993
So, it wasn't a bluff.

201
00:12:04,293 --> 00:12:05,705
He really is a beginner.

202
00:12:05,813 --> 00:12:06,953
This is too easy.

203
00:12:07,513 --> 00:12:10,050
In the same way a judo pro
can gauge his opponent's

204
00:12:10,133 --> 00:12:12,630
skill simply by looking at
the way he wears his gi,

205
00:12:12,713 --> 00:12:14,533
I can read him like a book.

206
00:12:14,813 --> 00:12:18,653
And chapter one is called
Jotaro, the Video Game Novice.

207
00:12:19,453 --> 00:12:22,553
All the same, I refuse
to let my guard down.

208
00:12:23,573 --> 00:12:26,926
I'm aware of the weaknesses
of every batter in this game.

209
00:12:27,493 --> 00:12:29,846
Next will be a low pitch to the outside.

210
00:12:30,553 --> 00:12:35,073
I'll throw my best pitch, the
four-seam fastball, and strike him out.

211
00:12:35,393 --> 00:12:36,687
It's the first inning.

212
00:12:36,953 --> 00:12:39,273
Two outs, two strikes, and no fouls.

213
00:12:39,413 --> 00:12:40,884
Here comes my next pitch.

214
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:41,975
Go right ahead.

215
00:12:42,453 --> 00:12:46,218
I've pretty much gotten the hang
of batting with the controller.

216
00:12:46,493 --> 00:12:48,213
Wait, what did he just say?

217
00:12:48,453 --> 00:12:50,100
I must have heard him wrong.

218
00:12:50,933 --> 00:12:53,168
What does he mean, got the hang of it?

219
00:12:55,153 --> 00:12:57,353
Surely he couldn't have...

220
00:12:58,573 --> 00:13:00,044
What is he talking about?

221
00:13:00,253 --> 00:13:01,353
What does he mean?

222
00:13:08,013 --> 00:13:08,843
What?!

223
00:13:08,926 --> 00:13:09,756
Jotaro!

224
00:13:10,173 --> 00:13:14,190
All right, I'm really starting to
enjoy this game. What in the...

225
00:13:14,273 --> 00:13:16,413
It can't be! It's going!

226
00:13:16,753 --> 00:13:18,353
The ball is still going!

227
00:13:18,933 --> 00:13:20,521
It just doesn't make sense.

228
00:13:20,713 --> 00:13:23,066
What did he mean by, got the hang of it?

229
00:13:23,233 --> 00:13:24,533
Got the hang of it?

230
00:13:24,893 --> 00:13:26,373
Got the hang of it?

231
00:13:27,973 --> 00:13:28,803
Ah!

232
00:13:29,853 --> 00:13:30,683
He...

233
00:13:30,766 --> 00:13:31,596
He did it!

234
00:13:31,679 --> 00:13:34,170
I don't know how, but he did it!

235
00:13:34,253 --> 00:13:35,853
Ha ha ha ha ha!

236
00:13:37,013 --> 00:13:37,843
Haruno!

237
00:13:44,533 --> 00:13:45,713
Home run!

238
00:13:46,153 --> 00:13:47,553
It's a home run!

239
00:13:48,053 --> 00:13:49,693
Ha ha ha ha ha!

240
00:13:50,593 --> 00:13:52,553
Jotaro! Damn you!

241
00:14:03,053 --> 00:14:03,883
Jotaro!

242
00:14:03,966 --> 00:14:06,833
Did I really hear you
correctly? Say something!

243
00:14:07,173 --> 00:14:10,170
It sounded like you've pretty
much gotten the hang of batting!

244
00:14:10,253 --> 00:14:12,373
I don't feel like repeating myself.

245
00:14:14,753 --> 00:14:17,210
He was a beginner when
we started this game,

246
00:14:17,293 --> 00:14:19,630
and yet he's claiming
to have learned proper

247
00:14:19,713 --> 00:14:22,125
swinging technique in only eight pitches!

248
00:14:22,833 --> 00:14:26,853
Jotaro Kuto has all the speed
and dexterity of Star Platinum.

249
00:14:27,593 --> 00:14:32,181
Now I know why Master Dio finds him to
be problematic and why my brother lost.

250
00:14:37,873 --> 00:14:38,703
Interesting.

251
00:14:38,933 --> 00:14:41,850
I couldn't have asked for
a more fitting opponent.

252
00:14:41,933 --> 00:14:44,653
But as naturally gifted as you may be,

253
00:14:44,893 --> 00:14:49,305
you made a critical mistake by revealing
your talents so early in the game.

254
00:14:49,613 --> 00:14:52,593
A mistake that will cost you dearly.

255
00:14:55,653 --> 00:14:57,713
Let's resume the game, Jotaro.

256
00:15:03,093 --> 00:15:04,693
Yes, he did it!

257
00:15:05,293 --> 00:15:06,573
That's my boy!

258
00:15:06,893 --> 00:15:09,187
Another home run right out of the park!

259
00:15:09,413 --> 00:15:10,853
Talk about a comeback!

260
00:15:11,333 --> 00:15:12,970
Four runs in the first inning!

261
00:15:13,053 --> 00:15:16,053
Looks like you've got this
game in the bag, Jotaro!

262
00:15:16,153 --> 00:15:18,977
Keep it up, and we'll be
out of here in no time.

263
00:15:19,473 --> 00:15:24,673
Hey, Darby, you'll just ignore me, but
I'll say it anyway because I'm a nice guy.

264
00:15:25,093 --> 00:15:26,350
I'm giving you an out.

265
00:15:26,433 --> 00:15:30,990
All you have to do is return Kakyoin's soul
and take us to Dio of your own volition.

266
00:15:31,073 --> 00:15:33,544
If you cooperate, no harm will befall you.

267
00:15:38,933 --> 00:15:39,763
Huh?

268
00:15:40,553 --> 00:15:43,590
For all his faults, my
brother was a master gambler.

269
00:15:43,673 --> 00:15:46,073
He made conning people into an art form.

270
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:50,590
You'd think his younger brother
would be perfect to practice on.

271
00:15:50,673 --> 00:15:51,953
But you'd be wrong.

272
00:15:52,213 --> 00:15:54,710
He never asked me to
play one game of poker.

273
00:15:54,793 --> 00:15:58,734
No, I was never asked to play any
games of the gambling persuasion.

274
00:15:58,973 --> 00:16:00,453
Any guesses why?

275
00:16:02,513 --> 00:16:03,733
When I was 15,

276
00:16:04,013 --> 00:16:08,070
I caught my brother putting his
oh-so-predictable moves on my girlfriend.

277
00:16:08,153 --> 00:16:10,990
He was 10 years older, but
I beat him to a bloody pulp.

278
00:16:11,073 --> 00:16:15,113
I broke his ribs and proceeded
to kick him until he spat blood.

279
00:16:15,413 --> 00:16:18,790
The last thing my brother said
to me was how sorry he was.

280
00:16:18,873 --> 00:16:20,213
Any idea why?

281
00:16:20,733 --> 00:16:23,170
Would you please cut to the chase already?

282
00:16:23,253 --> 00:16:24,083
Even as kids,

283
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:25,950
my brother had the good sense to realize

284
00:16:26,033 --> 00:16:28,470
that he'd never have
what it took to beat me.

285
00:16:28,553 --> 00:16:31,847
The reason for that is about
to become abundantly clear.

286
00:16:32,773 --> 00:16:37,830
At this moment, you have a false sense of
confidence due to the home run you hit.

287
00:16:37,913 --> 00:16:42,325
But deep down, you feel a sense of
unease, not unlike what my brother felt.

288
00:16:42,553 --> 00:16:45,318
My prowess is beginning
to worry you, isn't it?

289
00:16:45,613 --> 00:16:49,670
Right now, you're coming to a daunting
conclusion about the game's outcome,

290
00:16:49,753 --> 00:16:50,893
aren't you, Jotaro?

291
00:16:51,253 --> 00:16:53,371
What the hell are you talking about?

292
00:16:55,333 --> 00:16:56,392
Changing pictures!

293
00:16:56,813 --> 00:16:59,633
Number 15 is out and number 77 is in!

294
00:17:00,133 --> 00:17:05,333
77 is a power pitcher with a max pitch
speed of 165 kilometers per hour!

295
00:17:06,813 --> 00:17:07,643
Also...

296
00:17:07,913 --> 00:17:09,972
I'll tell you the pitch I'll throw.

297
00:17:10,613 --> 00:17:15,133
Number 77 will throw a forkball, and
he'll throw it right down the middle.

298
00:17:15,573 --> 00:17:16,773
What the hell?

299
00:17:17,253 --> 00:17:19,350
Why would he declare what he's throwing?

300
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:22,310
A forkball is about to
come barreling down center.

301
00:17:22,393 --> 00:17:24,217
But will you believe me or not?

302
00:17:24,753 --> 00:17:27,830
Jotaro, he's just spouting
nonsense to shake your confidence.

303
00:17:27,913 --> 00:17:30,854
Do yourself a favor and
ignore everything he says.

304
00:17:31,113 --> 00:17:32,653
Throw it, Derby.

305
00:17:33,413 --> 00:17:35,773
Will you believe or will you doubt?

306
00:17:41,793 --> 00:17:42,833
I knew it.

307
00:17:42,993 --> 00:17:45,470
It's a fastball, and
it's coming right at you.

308
00:17:45,553 --> 00:17:46,383
Let's see.

309
00:17:46,466 --> 00:17:48,250
Is the ball going to change direction?

310
00:17:48,333 --> 00:17:50,553
The suspense is driving me crazy.

311
00:17:52,033 --> 00:17:53,073
You swung.

312
00:17:53,313 --> 00:17:55,750
You bought his act and
bet on the forkball.

313
00:17:55,833 --> 00:17:56,833
It's still going.

314
00:17:57,093 --> 00:17:58,933
It actually is a fastball.

315
00:17:59,993 --> 00:18:00,853
Oh, great.

316
00:18:00,993 --> 00:18:02,758
He hit the bottom of the ball.

317
00:18:04,413 --> 00:18:05,243
Out.

318
00:18:05,693 --> 00:18:07,953
First inning, three outs change!

319
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:13,913
Idiot! How could you?

320
00:18:14,233 --> 00:18:16,530
Leave it to a rookie
for something like that!

321
00:18:16,613 --> 00:18:19,025
I can't believe you swung for a forkball!

322
00:18:21,573 --> 00:18:22,403
No.

323
00:18:22,486 --> 00:18:26,190
He had already seen through me and knew
I would swing expecting a forkball.

324
00:18:26,273 --> 00:18:28,413
So we switched it up to a fastball.

325
00:18:28,753 --> 00:18:30,341
But he has a point, though.

326
00:18:30,633 --> 00:18:34,010
Something's been gnawing at me ever
since we stepped foot in this mansion.

327
00:18:34,093 --> 00:18:35,293
I'm not sure how,

328
00:18:35,633 --> 00:18:40,104
but he knew Star Platinum would throw
a right punch in our earlier skirmish.

329
00:18:40,573 --> 00:18:41,403
What?

330
00:18:41,486 --> 00:18:42,316
Impossible!

331
00:18:42,399 --> 00:18:44,330
Are you trying to tell me
that he can read your mind?

332
00:18:44,413 --> 00:18:46,884
No offense, Jotaro, but that's crazy talk!

333
00:18:48,173 --> 00:18:49,761
Oh, would you look at that?

334
00:18:49,973 --> 00:18:51,233
It's my turn at bat.

335
00:19:01,073 --> 00:19:02,973
This is going to be a home run.

336
00:19:03,653 --> 00:19:08,418
Keep your eye on the birdie, as I'll be
hitting it into the left field bleachers!

337
00:19:09,653 --> 00:19:14,390
Old man, are you absolutely sure the game
and console haven't been tampered with?

338
00:19:14,473 --> 00:19:16,070
Yeah, I'm positive it's clean.

339
00:19:16,153 --> 00:19:17,313
And that's not all.

340
00:19:17,533 --> 00:19:20,533
I haven't seen him make a
single funny move either.

341
00:19:20,633 --> 00:19:23,170
Then his secret weapon has
to be that stand of his.

342
00:19:23,253 --> 00:19:25,110
His stand doesn't just take souls.

343
00:19:25,193 --> 00:19:27,075
It must have some other ability.

344
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:31,028
This'll be my target.

345
00:19:34,853 --> 00:19:36,912
Now I'll get to the bottom of this.

346
00:19:37,373 --> 00:19:38,913
Has he lost his mind?

347
00:19:39,133 --> 00:19:41,670
He's going to try to hit
the banner on purpose?

348
00:19:41,753 --> 00:19:44,253
And where might you be aiming now, Jotaro?

349
00:19:44,673 --> 00:19:45,793
An inside pitch?

350
00:19:46,173 --> 00:19:47,613
Will you throw it high?

351
00:19:47,913 --> 00:19:49,153
Or low, perhaps?

352
00:19:49,533 --> 00:19:52,827
Or maybe you're planning some
kind of underhanded trick?

353
00:19:53,573 --> 00:19:54,403
Well...

354
00:20:01,933 --> 00:20:02,773
What the?

355
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:05,581
He pulled back with
Jotaro through the ball!

356
00:20:10,153 --> 00:20:10,983
He...

357
00:20:11,066 --> 00:20:12,150
predicted it! He...

358
00:20:12,233 --> 00:20:14,773
knew exactly what would happen! But how?

359
00:20:15,073 --> 00:20:19,110
There's no way he could have seen that
pitch coming unless he read Jotaro's mind!

360
00:20:19,193 --> 00:20:20,053
Home run!

361
00:20:23,873 --> 00:20:24,893
That's one run.

362
00:20:25,593 --> 00:20:26,853
Damn this bastard!

363
00:20:27,353 --> 00:20:29,910
We faced all kinds of
opponents on this journey,

364
00:20:29,993 --> 00:20:32,130
but never one who can read our minds!

365
00:20:32,213 --> 00:20:36,110
If he really can read minds, then it
doesn't matter how clever we think we are.

366
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:38,722
We won't stand a
snowball's chance in hell!

367
00:20:39,213 --> 00:20:41,193
Jotaro, what are you going to do?

368
00:20:54,213 --> 00:21:01,213
why that damn the punks declaring another
home run let's see uh-huh an outside pitch

369
00:21:02,193 --> 00:21:05,250
or maybe you're going
to aim low or something

370
00:21:18,273 --> 00:21:19,313
Home run!

371
00:21:20,433 --> 00:21:21,673
Four to two.

372
00:21:23,953 --> 00:21:24,783
Damn!

373
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:27,870
A person's body language and
the surrounding environment go

374
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,910
a long way toward helping
predict an opponent's next move.

375
00:21:30,993 --> 00:21:33,050
But there's no way to do it perfectly!

376
00:21:33,133 --> 00:21:37,213
And yet, his stand predicts
Jotaro's pitch with 100 % accuracy.

377
00:21:37,593 --> 00:21:39,652
And technically, he's not cheating.

378
00:21:41,473 --> 00:21:42,553
Another home run!

379
00:21:42,813 --> 00:21:43,873
It's 4-3!

380
00:21:44,513 --> 00:21:47,590
How are we supposed to stop
him from reading our minds?

381
00:21:47,673 --> 00:21:48,503
How?

382
00:21:52,173 --> 00:21:54,893
At this rate, I'll be
in the lead in no time.

383
00:21:55,133 --> 00:21:56,133
Now, what's next?

384
00:21:56,293 --> 00:22:00,313
An inside pitch, a fastball, a
high pitch, or maybe a curveball?

385
00:22:00,633 --> 00:22:01,927
What's up your sleeve?

386
00:22:05,853 --> 00:22:10,650
huh your hat huh you
idiot do you honestly take

387
00:22:10,733 --> 00:22:13,380
me for a cheat like my
ne 'er-do-well brother

388
00:22:13,613 --> 00:22:16,570
Jotaro you've got it wrong
hiding your face is useless

389
00:22:16,653 --> 00:22:19,490
I don't know what he's doing
but he's not watching the

390
00:22:19,573 --> 00:22:22,570
reflection of the screen in
your eyes I get that it's hard

391
00:22:22,653 --> 00:22:25,750
not to go there now but there's
no way he can see what you're

392
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:28,590
pressing or what pitch you're
choosing trust me I've been

393
00:22:28,673 --> 00:22:31,870
watching him the entire time
that's not what's been going on

394
00:22:31,953 --> 00:22:35,390
here i only took off my hat
because i'm sweating no other

395
00:22:35,473 --> 00:22:39,133
reason huh could you throw your
next pitch sometime this year

396
00:22:40,673 --> 00:22:47,150
but i'm not going to be sweating anymore
i'll tell you my next pitch i'm throwing

397
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:52,910
a high outside fastball you're joking
dotero do you hear what you're saying

398
00:22:52,993 --> 00:22:58,950
right now of course i do finally starting
to lose your hearing old man obviously

399
00:22:59,033 --> 00:23:03,993
i just told him my next pitch a high
outside fastball that's how i'm gonna win

400
00:23:08,933 --> 00:23:09,763
jotaro

401
00:23:13,453 --> 00:23:16,613
will you believe me or will you doubt me

402
00:23:19,793 --> 00:23:21,573
you're not too bright are you

403
00:23:28,353 --> 00:23:31,550
do you hear what you're saying
right now obviously i just told him

404
00:23:31,633 --> 00:23:35,550
my next pitch what the hell he's
telling the truth yes you tampered

405
00:23:35,633 --> 00:23:38,850
with the console no it must have
something to do with that hat of

406
00:23:38,933 --> 00:23:42,874
yours this is just a dance of
deception where the loser cries first
